{"ts": 0.033479, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J", "len": 11}
{"ts": 0.034713, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshelltutor\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule : shells\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--------------------------------------------\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 138}
{"ts": 0.034796, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mshells: what runs your commands\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThree short lessons, then a task. This module stands alone and saves\r\nnothing. You'll look at the shell as a program, at other shells, and\r\n", "len": 186}
{"ts": 0.034852, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "at the difference between your login shell and this one.\r\n\r\nAssumes the five stages, or that you know \u001b[92mls\u001b[0m, \u001b[92mcd\u001b[0m and \u001b[92m>\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m> Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m for lesson 1.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 194}
{"ts": 0.038251, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
{"ts": 0.038477, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 91}
{"ts": 0.038495, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.053215, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004hshelltutor> ", "len": 20}
{"ts": 0.053347, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "next\n", "len": 5}
{"ts": 0.05338, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "next\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r", "len": 15}
{"ts": 0.05919, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J", "len": 11}
{"ts": 0.060593, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule\u001b[0m \u001b[90m-------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshells  1/3\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 127}
{"ts": 0.060638, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.0607, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mThe shell is a program\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThe shell reads your line, finds the program you named, and runs it.\r\n", "len": 107}
{"ts": 0.060717, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "It is itself a program, and you can look at it.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mecho $BASH_VERSION\u001b[0m     \u001b[90m# the version of the shell running now\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mps -o pid,comm\u001b[0m         \u001b[90m# the programs on this terminal, by name\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nTwo of those lines are shells: the tutor's own, and the one you are\r\ntyping into. \u001b[92m$BASH_VERSION\u001b[0m is a \u001b[1mvariable\u001b[0m: a name that holds a value.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m> Run both, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 429}
{"ts": 0.064088, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
{"ts": 0.064315, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 91}
{"ts": 0.064331, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.078525, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004hshelltutor> ", "len": 20}
{"ts": 0.078623, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "next\n", "len": 5}
{"ts": 0.078651, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "next\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r", "len": 15}
{"ts": 0.083644, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J", "len": 11}
{"ts": 0.085123, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule\u001b[0m \u001b[90m-------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshells  2/3\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 127}
{"ts": 0.085175, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.085228, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mOther shells exist\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 33}
{"ts": 0.085243, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[92mbash\u001b[0m is common on Linux and is what this tutor runs. \u001b[92mzsh\u001b[0m is the\r\ndefault on macOS. \u001b[92mfish\u001b[0m is another, installed separately.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mcommand -v zsh fish\u001b[0m     \u001b[90m# one path for each that is installed\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nNo line for a shell means it is not installed. That is normal. What\r\ndiffers between shells is setup and prompt; \u001b[92mls\u001b[0m, paths and pipes are\r\nthe same in all of them.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m> Run it, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 458}
{"ts": 0.085264, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.088766, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
{"ts": 0.088987, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 91}
{"ts": 0.089001, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.103086, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004hshelltutor> ", "len": 20}
{"ts": 0.103179, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "next\n", "len": 5}
{"ts": 0.103206, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "next\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r", "len": 15}
{"ts": 0.108588, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J", "len": 11}
{"ts": 0.109979, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule\u001b[0m \u001b[90m-------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshells  3/3\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 127}
{"ts": 0.110066, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.110107, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mYour login shell and this shell\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nYour \u001b[1mlogin shell\u001b[0m is the one a new terminal window starts. It can\r\n", "len": 120}
{"ts": 0.11013, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "differ from the shell running now.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mecho $SHELL\u001b[0m            \u001b[90m# your login shell\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mecho $BASH_VERSION\u001b[0m     \u001b[90m# the shell running now\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThis tutor always runs its lessons in bash, whatever your login shell\r\nis. What you practise here works the same under zsh.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m> Compare the two lines, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m for the task.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 374}
{"ts": 0.113491, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
{"ts": 0.113713, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 91}
{"ts": 0.113729, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.127658, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004hshelltutor> ", "len": 20}
{"ts": 0.127757, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "next\n", "len": 5}
{"ts": 0.127783, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "next\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r", "len": 15}
{"ts": 0.133124, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J", "len": 11}
{"ts": 0.134479, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule\u001b[0m \u001b[90m------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshells  gate\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 127}
{"ts": 0.134504, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.134532, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mshells — gate\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[36mRecall\u001b[0m (three questions, all three must be correct).\r\n", "len": 93}
{"ts": 0.134579, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "First, three questions. Type your answer in words; this is not the shell.\r\n\r\nThen a \u001b[36mpractical task\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n", "len": 112}
{"ts": 0.136575, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(the question again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 91}
{"ts": 0.136793, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 91}
{"ts": 0.136808, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.140528, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m 1 of 3   The shell runs the programs you name. What kind of thing is the\r\n", "len": 85}
{"ts": 0.140563, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "a program\n", "len": 10}
{"ts": 0.140587, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m          shell itself?\r\na program\r\n", "len": 46}
{"ts": 0.143489, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m          a program    a file    a folder    a window\r\n", "len": 65}
{"ts": 0.143508, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 12}
{"ts": 0.14352, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m| ?\u001b[0m ", "len": 13}
{"ts": 0.153271, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m \u001b[92m[x]\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 27}
{"ts": 0.157014, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m 2 of 3   What do you type to ask whether zsh is installed?\r\n", "len": 71}
{"ts": 0.157061, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "command -v zsh\n", "len": 15}
{"ts": 0.157086, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[93m| ?\u001b[0m command -v zsh\r\n", "len": 41}
{"ts": 0.166861, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m \u001b[92m[x]\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 27}
{"ts": 0.171016, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m 3 of 3   \u001b[92mecho $SHELL\u001b[0m prints which shell?\r\n", "len": 62}
{"ts": 0.171123, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "login shell\n", "len": 12}
{"ts": 0.171154, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "login shell\r\n", "len": 13}
{"ts": 0.174584, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m          the running one    your login shell    the newest one\r\n", "len": 75}
{"ts": 0.174637, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[93m| ?\u001b[0m ", "len": 25}
{"ts": 0.184531, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[93m|\u001b[0m \u001b[92m[x]\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 27}
{"ts": 0.196891, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J", "len": 11}
{"ts": 0.198393, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule\u001b[0m \u001b[90m------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshells  task\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 127}
{"ts": 0.198426, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.198487, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mshells — task\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 30}
{"ts": 0.198534, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "Find out whether \u001b[92mzsh\u001b[0m is installed, and keep the answer in a file.\r\n\r\n  1. Ask the shell where zsh is.\r\n  2. Send what it prints into a file named zsh.txt.\r\n\r\nIf zsh is not installed the file is empty, and that is a right answer.\r\n\u001b[90mThis task runs in the module's own folder; \u001b[92mpwd\u001b[90m shows it.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m> Do both steps, then type \u001b[92mcheck\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 374}
{"ts": 0.201164, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mcheck\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(test your work)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(the task again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 132}
{"ts": 0.201383, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 93}
{"ts": 0.215396, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004hshelltutor> ", "len": 20}
{"ts": 0.215528, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "command -v zsh > zsh.txt\n", "len": 25}
{"ts": 0.215571, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "command -v zsh > zsh.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r", "len": 35}
{"ts": 0.215888, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004h", "len": 8}
{"ts": 0.215902, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "shelltutor> ", "len": 12}
{"ts": 0.215924, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "check\n", "len": 6}
{"ts": 0.215944, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "check\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r", "len": 16}
{"ts": 0.236835, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J", "len": 11}
{"ts": 0.238304, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshelltutor\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule : shells\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--------------------------------------------\u001b[0m \u001b[90m--\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 136}
{"ts": 0.238354, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.238412, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mshells cleared.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nCommands and keys from this module:\r\n", "len": 67}
{"ts": 0.238456, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "  \u001b[92mecho $BASH_VERSION\u001b[0m \u001b[90mthe shell running now\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mps -o pid,comm\u001b[0m \u001b[90mthe programs on this terminal\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mcommand -v NAME\u001b[0m \u001b[90mis NAME installed, and where\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mecho $SHELL   \u001b[0m \u001b[90myour login shell\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m> Type \u001b[92mquit\u001b[93m to leave, or \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to start this module again.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 339}
{"ts": 0.241259, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(start this module again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(leave)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 134}
{"ts": 0.24148, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 91}
{"ts": 0.241494, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.255824, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004hshelltutor> ", "len": 20}
{"ts": 0.25594, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "quit\n", "len": 5}
{"ts": 0.255966, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "quit\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r", "len": 15}
{"ts": 0.25888, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J", "len": 11}
{"ts": 0.259059, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "Bye. A module saves nothing; run 'shelltutor shells' to start it again.\r\n", "len": 73}
